cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NucleOS or NucleScript in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NucleOS and NucleScript: a software-defined DNA storage engine and its language"
abstract: >-
  NucleOS encodes files into DNA strands and back: ternary, DNA Fountain,
  Yin-Yang and HEDGES codecs, Reed-Solomon parity planned from a measured
  channel, consensus and clustering of real sequencing reads, primer
  addressing and a versioned virtual filesystem, tested against a noise
  simulator with channels measured from real oligo pools. NucleScript,
  version 1.0, is its language: pools typed by sequencer profile and
  error rate, and effects for synthesis, sequencing and deletion whose
  confirmations are checked at compile time, run against the simulator,
  with order sheets for Twist and IDT and decoding of real reads at its
  edges.
authors:
